# Counter loop with a while condition

Verifies a `while` loop re-evaluates its boolean condition before every
iteration and stops when the condition becomes false, printing the values
0, 1, and 2 through the complete CLI pipeline.

>>> source
let i: int = 0

while (i < 3) {
    print(i)
    i = i + 1
}

<<< stdout
0
1
2

<<< stderr
